; A two-arm `T / null` choice whose non-`null` arm is a bare FIXED VALUE (`t = true / null`;
; equally `false / null`, `5 / null`, `-1 / null`, `3.0 / null`, `"v1" / null`, and the degenerate
; `null / null`) is REJECTED GRACEFULLY at the RULE-level collapse site (`parse_type_choices`), so
; the generator exits 1 with an actionable message rather than aborting.
;
; The refusal is what the shape actually means. A two-arm choice with a `null` arm never becomes an
; enum: it collapses to an `Option<T>` (that collapse is what makes `t = uint / null` an
; `Option<u64>` and `t = null / tstr` an `Option<String>`). A `Fixed` has no `T` — it exists only
; as an unstored member whose value the schema pins — so the collapse produces an
; `Optional(Fixed(..))` with nothing to put in the slot, and rendering a `Fixed` in member position
; is a hard abort at generation time. Refusing at the collapse itself is what keeps the diagnosis
; on the user's CDDL instead of on an internal render invariant.
;
; The message names the offending value back in its CDDL spelling and offers only a remedy that was
; probed to work: widening the fixed arm to the CDDL type the constant inhabits (`bool / null`
; lowers to `Option<bool>`; `uint / null` likewise) generates under both the default and
; `--preserve-encodings` profiles. It says plainly that widening drops the constraint, so the
; result is a different spec, not an equivalent one. The `null / null` spelling gets a different
; sentence, because there is no fixed value in the `T` slot at all — there is no non-`null` arm to
; widen, and a rule body of bare `null` is itself rejected at the alias seam.
;
; Neighbouring shapes that are deliberately NOT this class, and must stay as they are:
;   - `t = true / false` — no `null` arm, so no collapse; it becomes a `pub enum T { True, False }`.
;   - `t = null / tstr`, `t = uint / null` — a non-fixed inner collapses to a real `Option<T>`.
;   - `t = true / null / tstr` — THREE arms never reach the collapse; it takes the enum path and is
;     a separately tracked defect (see cddl-matrix/ROADMAP.md § findings), untouched by this guard.
; The MEMBER-position spelling of this same shape has its own collapse site and its own fixture,
; tests/robustness/choice_fixed_null_collapse_member.cddl.
;
; The second rule is deliberate: it proves the refusal fires on an otherwise-generatable spec, not
; only on a spec that has nothing else to emit.
a = [x: uint]
t = true / null
